{"source_slots":{"s4":"So if I go with a more compact model, would that still be sturdy enough for a couple of people? I don't want to sacrifice too much space for the sake of fitting in the compartment.","s5":""Yes, absolutely. A "compact" two-person model can be just as sturdy as a larger one, as long as the materials are high-quality nylon. You don't necessarily have to sacrifice too much space—you can still maintain a comfortable sleeping area while keeping the pack size small and light.

However, you'll want to ensure the *specific* model you select has a **good rating** (e.g., a 3-person rating or higher) so it remains robust for your use case. 

If you're prioritizing a specific footprint for the compartment, then look for the lightest 2-person tent model available!""}}
